-- title:
--   Adjacent edge charts generate the vertex chart ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible $\pi \in \mathcal O$ with $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$, and a field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ have matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$, let $n \in \mathbb N$, and write $A_n$ and $V_n$ for the quotients of the edge chart ring `chartERing 𝒪 π r` (the localisation away from `edgeQuot.discr 𝒪 π r`) and of the vertex chart ring `chartVRing 𝒪 r` (the localisation away from `vertexDiscr 𝒪 r`) by the ideals generated by $\pi^{n+1}$. Let $\iota : A_n \to V_n$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map carrying the class of $\xi$ to the class of $\zeta$ and with $\iota(\eta)\cdot\zeta = \pi$ in $V_n$. Let $k \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ fix the standard vertex $[\mathcal O^2]$ but not the vertex $g_1\cdot[\mathcal O^2]$, and let $\tau$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $V_n$ with the following transport property: for every commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $y : V_n \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, d'$ over $B$ for $(K_0,\pi)$, if $d$ has line $B\cdot(y(\zeta)\otimes e_0 + 1\otimes e_1)$ at the standard full lattice $L_0$ and line the image under `actBaseChange` of $B\cdot(y(\zeta)\otimes e_0 + \pi\otimes e_1)$ at $g_1 L_0$, and `InEdgeChart` holds for $d$ at the pair $(g_1L_0, L_0)$ (that is, `EdgeNondegAt` at every prime of $B$), and if $d'$ satisfies the same three conditions with $y$ replaced by $y\circ\tau$, then $d'$ is the pullback of $d$ along $k^{-1}$, i.e. $d'.\mathrm{line}(M)$ is the preimage of $d.\mathrm{line}(k^{-1}M)$ under the base-changed lattice map for every full lattice $M$. Then the images of $\iota$ and of $\tau\circ\iota$ generate $V_n$: their join as $\mathcal O$-subalgebras is all of $V_n$.
--
--   In Mumford's formal model of the $p$-adic upper half plane, the two edge charts attached to two edges meeting at a common vertex overlap in the vertex region, and the assertion here is that the vertex chart ring is generated by the two resulting copies of the edge chart ring; equivalently, the overlap $\operatorname{Spec} V_n \to \operatorname{Spec} A_n \times \operatorname{Spec} A_n$ is a closed immersion. It feeds the separatedness of the glued formal scheme, used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.isSeparated_of_mumfordGlueLaws`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.isSeparated_of_mumfordGlueLaws).
